.TH SETREGID 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
setregid \- sets the real and effective group ids; (gid_t)-1 leaves an id unchanged
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B int setregid(gid_t real, gid_t effective);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets the real and effective group IDs; (gid_t)-1 leaves an ID unchanged. This is a direct per-thread syscall.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result on success, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setregid (2)
